  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Weather remains quiet through Friday, rain chances \nreturn this weekend.\n\nQuiet weather is expected for today through the end of the week, due \nto surface high pressure and ridging aloft. Temperatures stay in\nthe 70s/80s, right around normal for this time of year. Dewpoints\nin the 50s to low 60s will make the air feel drier and more \npleasant for late July standards. Northwesterly winds will \nremain elevated today, gusting to around 20-25 mph in the higher\nelevations, lowering slightly to 15-20 mph for Thursday before \nbecoming light Friday. Temperatures will remain near to slightly\nbelow normal, with highs in the 70s/80s, with similar \ntemperatures through the end of the week. \n\nRain chances stay away until Saturday, when the high shifts east, \nallowing for southerly flow to return to the area. This will \nincrease moisture ahead of the next system moving into the area from \nthe Great Plains along with an upper level trough. Scattered to \nwidespread showers and storms return Saturday afternoon, continuing \neach day into next week, due to consistent upper-level troughing \nover the Eastern CONUS and southerly flow at the surface. Due to \nincreased cloud cover and rain chances, temperatures remain \nrelatively cool, with highs in the 70s to low 80s through the middle \nof next week.",
